      },
      "lineNbr": 127,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-07T21:07:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can be replaced with \n\n    if (fColor.fA !\u003d 1.0) { \n        AddColorBlendBlock(keyContext, builder, gatherer, SkBlendMode::kDstIn, {0, 0, 0, fColor.fA});\n    }\n    \nWhether or not we replace this, I realize we are making one pipeline for a paint with no extra alpha multiply and another pipeline for the same paint and the alpha multiply. We also have to add a blend mode uniform that will always be set to kDstIn (there\u0027s a similar issue with the `BlendModeShader` use for passthrough blenders that always uploads kSrcOver). The snippets aren\u0027t set up for it but it would be nice if these specific cases could use `kFixedFunctionSrcOverBlendMode` etc.\n\nAs-is, though, just adding the block directly is equivalent to what we currently do but avoids creating an SkColorFilter on the heap and a virtual call.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 127,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "3899307a252ce270745133d5483b062b41ad9d48",
